# Resource scripts are stored as UTF-16LE. Git's eol conversion (core.autocrlf)
# rewrites the 0x0A low byte of a UTF-16 LF into a raw CRLF, which misaligns the
# rest of the file and silently corrupts it on checkout. Marking them -text
# disables that conversion while keeping the UTF-16LE diff driver so they still
# produce readable diffs.
*.rc -text diff=UTF-16LE
*.rc2 -text diff=UTF-16LE

# Visual Studio resource editor working files are binary
*.aps binary

# Signing certificates and key files are binary
*.pfx binary
*.snk binary
